// [M-module-file-submodule-split-silent-orphan] repro fixture, orphan half.
//
// Declares the SAME `module module_file_orphan_repro.core` as `core.nv`,
// but sits directly beside it under its OWN name (`scattered.nv`) — not
// inside a dedicated `core/` folder-module. Its own filename does not
// match the module's last segment (`core`), so it can never be the
// resolved head-file of a plain `import module_file_orphan_repro.core`,
// and there is no `core/` folder for it to be a legitimate folder-module
// peer of either. This is the orphan: any importer of
// `module_file_orphan_repro.core` other than this file itself resolves to
// `core.nv` alone — `scattered_value` below is invisible to them, which
// `resolve_module_paths` must now catch as `[E_MODULE_FILE_ORPHAN]`
// instead of silently dropping it (pre-Plan-202 behaviour) or silently
// merging it in without diagnostic (reverted masking fix
// `[M-blanket-crossmodule-scattered-peer-drop]`).
module module_file_orphan_repro.core

export fn scattered_value() -> int => 2
